      "content": "thanks. u mentioned drill has \"street roots\" and AAVE slang needs to be used \"cautiously.\" i'm trying to get more specific for the client. when u say \"cautiously,\" do u mean it's kind of risky because it can come across as unrefined or \"low-class\" if a high-end brand uses it wrong? and regarding drill vs the clean girl thing, would u say the drill/AAVE stuff is inherently more associated with \"street-level\" demographics whereas the clean girl aesthetic is more \"aspirational\" or upper-class? just trying to see if there's a clear distinction in the \"social class\" they represent.",
